From b39441a16f967229bbf5b6ff33c1e4a0dc9b3b5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joey Riches <josephriches@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 15:43:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] sax: Use LUTs for character classification

Previously, the parser consisted of a big ol' while loop that was
iterated on byte by byte, where each byte had to be matched against several
if/switch cases.

By introducing LUTs, we can continually iterate over chucks until we do
find a special character, then handle it explicitly, instead of
checking byte by byte.

This avoids expensive branch mispredictions and allows the parser to
stay in a 'happy path' for a longer period of time.

A python script is also provided for LUT generation and validation; also
as a means to easily build modified LUTs if they ever need to be
adjusted.
